    "q-79748": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79748",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Given a rectangular solid, find the differential $\\text{d}S$ for the surface area $S$ of the rectangular solid if the lengths of the sides are $a=4,$ $b=5,$ and $c=7.$",
      "worked_solution": "The  surface area of the rectangular solid is $S=2ab+2bc+2ac.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(a,b,c) & =(\\frac{∂S}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂S}{∂b})\\,\\text{d}b+(\\frac{∂S}{∂c})\\,\\text{d}c \\\\  & =2(b+c)\\,\\text{d}a+2(a+c)\\,\\text{d}b+2(a+b)\\,\\text{d}c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=4,$ $b=5,$ and $c=7,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(4,5,7) & =2(5+7)\\,\\text{d}a+2(4+7)\\,\\text{d}b+2(4+5)\\,\\text{d}c \\\\  & =24\\,\\text{d}a+22\\,\\text{d}b+18\\,\\text{d}c.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
