    "q-167168": {
      "dom_id": "step-q167168",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "If $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz),$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y,z)$ from $(1,1,1)$ to $(2,3,4).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y+\\frac{1}{z}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(1,1,1),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(1,1,1) & =1\\,\\text{d}x+1\\,\\text{d}y+1\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(1+Δx,1+Δy,1+Δz),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈Δx+Δy+Δz.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(1,1,1)$ to $(2,3,4),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =2-1=1, \\\\ Δy & =3-1=2 \\\\ Δz & =4-1=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈Δx+Δy+Δz \\\\  & ≈1+2+3 \\\\  & ≈6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y,z)$ increases by approximately $6.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
